# Universal Book Translator - environment file
#
# Copy to `.env` in the directory you run `ubt` from. Only UBT_-prefixed names
# are read from this file; an exported shell variable always wins over it.
#
# Provider API keys are the exception: they are read from the real environment
# only (`export OPENAI_API_KEY=...`), never from this file, because the
# credential lookup deliberately ignores un-prefixed names in a dotenv.
#
# If an existing `.env` already carries a bare `OPENAI_API_KEY=` /
# `OPENCODE_API_KEY=` line, it is ignored: move it to `UBT_LLM_API_KEY=` below
# (stays in this file) or export it from the shell.

# -- Outbound LLM credential (export one of these, or use a provider profile) --
#   OPENCODE_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / GEMINI_API_KEY
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, or a profile in ubt.toml / ~/.ubt/config.toml
# UBT_LLM_API_KEY=sk-...

# -- Models and protocol ------------------------------------------------------
# The defaults below are the author's benchmark targets, not a recommendation:
# name the model your credential can actually reach.
UBT_DRAFT_MODEL=muse-spark-1.3-contributor
UBT_REPAIR_MODEL=muse-spark-1.3-contributor
# chat (OpenAI/Gemini/DeepSeek-compatible) | responses | anthropic
# Leave this commented out: with no explicit api_mode the config auto-detects
# (anthropic base_url -> anthropic; muse-* draft/repair model -> responses).
# Setting UBT_API_MODE=chat here would pin the protocol and defeat that probe,
# which breaks muse-* models — they speak the Responses API, not chat.
# Only uncomment when you deliberately need the chat wire protocol.
# UBT_API_MODE=chat
# UBT_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# -- Inbound API auth (opt-in; required to bind anywhere but loopback) --------
# UBT_API_KEY=...
# UBT_ALLOWED_DIRS=/srv/books

# -- Run behaviour ------------------------------------------------------------
# UBT_RATE_LIMIT_RPM=60
# UBT_MAX_CONCURRENCY=10   (field is max_concurrency; there is no UBT_CONCURRENCY alias)
# UBT_QE_THRESHOLD=0.75
# UBT_RENDER_ENGINE=auto
# Opt out of the budget fail-closed preflight: keep running a capped job even
# when a model has no price-table entry (its spend then reports as unknown and
# the cap cannot fire). Default false = such jobs refuse to start.
# UBT_ALLOW_UNPRICED_BUDGET=false
# Local VLM OCR (deepseek-ocr) runs the checkpoint's own Python via
# transformers trust_remote_code — code from a downloaded repo, in this
# process. Default false refuses model-supplied code (the driver fails closed
# and points at a vetted offline snapshot); set true to opt in.
# UBT_VLM_TRUST_REMOTE_CODE=false

# System binaries this project calls but does not bundle: typst (required for
# any PDF render), poppler (visual gate + diagram SVG), node (MathJax formula
# backend), and a CJK font (Noto Serif/Sans CJK). `ubt doctor` checks all four.
